  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Hemarthria altissima",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemarthria_altissima",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1314303232,
      "text": "Hemarthria altissima, variously called limpo grass, limpograss, halt grass, Batavian quick grass, swamp couch grass, red swamp grass and red vleigrass, is a species of flowering plant in the jointgrass genus Hemarthria, family Poaceae. It is native to the Old World Tropics and Subtropics; Africa, Southern Europe, the Middle East, India, Southeast Asia, eastern China, and Borneo, and widely introduced as a forage in the New World, from Texas and Florida south to northern Argentina. In addition to being a valued forage for livestock, it makes a good, fragrant silage. A number of cultivars are commercially available."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Hemarthria altissima",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemarthria_altissima",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 29432269,
      "text": "Hemarthria altissima, yang secara beragam disebut sebagai limpo grass, limpograss, halt grass, Batavian quick grass, swamp couch grass, red swamp grass dan red vleigrass, adalah spesies tumbuhan berbunga dalam genus rumput sendi Hemarthria, keluarga Poaceae. Tumbuhan ini berasal dari wilayah Tropis dan Subtropis Dunia Lama; Afrika, Eropa Selatan, Timur Tengah, India, Asia Tenggara, Tiongkok bagian timur, dan Kalimantan, serta diperkenalkan secara luas sebagai tanaman pakan ternak di Dunia Baru, dari Texas dan Florida ke selatan hingga Argentina utara. Selain menjadi pakan ternak yang bernilai, tumbuhan ini juga menghasilkan silase yang baik dan harum. Sejumlah kultivar tersedia secara komersial."
    }
  },
